# Docs: user-guide + feature docs (together)

When you **implement or update a product feature** (UI, API, RBAC, or flows
users can see), treat documentation as part of delivery — not a follow-up.

Quality gates for code (dedupe offer + unit tests) stay in
`.cursor/rules/07-qa-dev-member.mdc`. This rule covers **docs only**.

## Dual update (required)

For user-facing behavior changes, update **both** when applicable:

| Layer | Where | Audience |
| ----- | ----- | -------- |
| **Dev / feature docs** | `docs/features/<area>/…`, plus auth/architecture guides if needed | Engineers |
| **User guide** | `docs/user-guide/<topic>/…` + `docs/docs-publish.json` if new pages | End users (prod `/docs`) |

Do **not** only update engineering docs and leave the user guide stale (or the
reverse).

## When this applies

- New screens, flows, filters, roles, or settings users interact with
- Behavior changes that alter steps, labels, who can access what, or outcomes
- Fixes that change the documented user path (not one-line typos in code)

## When to skip

- Pure refactors with no user-visible behavior change
- Test-only, tooling, CI, or cursor/rule/skill edits
- Internal-only APIs with no product surface (still update `docs/features/` if
  engineers need it; skip user-guide)

## Authoring checklist

1. Prefer **Living** prose in the user guide (steps, tables, related links) —
   match tone of existing `docs/user-guide/**` pages (no stub TODOs for shipped
   behavior).
2. Align UI labels and routes with the app (`/board`, **Allowlist**, etc.).
3. Reflect **RBAC** accurately (`minimumRole` in `docs-publish.json` when a page
   is manager/admin-only).
4. New user-guide page → add it under the right topic in
   `docs/docs-publish.json` (`path`, `order`, optional `minimumRole`).
5. Cross-link related user-guide pages; link from feature README to the
   user-guide topic when helpful.
6. After markdown edits: `pnpm --filter web docs:sync` (or rely on
   `predev`/`prebuild`).

## Finish the turn

If you shipped user-facing behavior and docs were in scope, briefly note what
user-guide / feature docs you updated (or why docs were skipped).

## Related

